# Action game — do not playtest as the agent

StarLance is a Phaser canvas **action video game** (timing, feel, thumbs, keyboard). The agent is not capable of testing it as a player.

## Do not

- Drive gameplay with Cursor browser tools, device emulation, synthetic pointer/touch/keyboard events, or CDP input
- Treat canvas screenshots, accessibility snapshots, or “phone viewport” chrome as a playtest
- Keep retrying when those methods fail — they cannot succeed for this game
- Claim controls, combat, or feel are verified after agent-side probing

## Do

- Implement from code and the request; check that input is wired (handlers exist, keyboard still works in code)
- Start the dev server only if needed to confirm the app boots — that is not a playtest
- State clearly what is unverified and that a human must try it (desktop keyboard and a real phone)
- Stop after implementation; wait for player notes instead of inventing a test loop

User rules about “verify web UI in the browser” do **not** apply to playing this game.
